<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">delete</ansi>

Delete your character for good and start a new one, keeping your login.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">delete character</ansi>

You're told what will be lost, then asked for your password (it isn't
shown as you type), then for your character's name. Only both together
delete. Any other answer cancels: "Nothing was deleted." (Pressing Enter
on its own just asks again.)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What goes, and what stays</ansi>

Everything about the character goes: their level and experience, gear,
gold and bank balance, company and companions, camp, horses, cargo,
standing, and tutorial progress. Nothing is dropped where you stood, so
nothing reaches another character.

Your login stays: your username and password, your settings (prompt,
colours, screen reader), macros, and aliases. You go straight into
making a new character, on the same connection, and the old name is free
at once, for you or anyone.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">When you can't</ansi>

Not in a fight or a battle, not while you're down, not as a practice
character in a tutorial replay, and not before you've made a character.
Travelling, camping, resting at an inn, riding, or with companions out
is fine.

Three wrong passwords in a row, here or in <ansi fg="command">password</ansi>, lock both
commands until you next log in.

This can't be undone.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help password</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help quit</ansi>.
